<h2>The conviction under appeal</h2>
<p>The Fast Track Special Court (POCSO) at Haridwar convicted the appellant on 17 October 2023 in a case that combined kidnapping-related charges under Sections 363 and 366A IPC, assault and intimidation counts under Sections 323, 504 and 506, outraging modesty under Section 354, an offence under Section 370(4), and aggravated sexual assault punished under Section 10 read with Section 9 of the POCSO Act. The operative sentence was five years rigorous imprisonment with a fine of Rs 5,000. The appeal against that conviction was filed through jail in 2023 and has not yet been heard on merits.</p>

<h2>The arithmetic that decided the application</h2>
<table class="law">
  <tr><th>Figure</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Sentence</td><td>Five years rigorous imprisonment with fine</td></tr>
